infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Extras vs dependency groups
  desc Two mechanisms, two audiences — routinely confused
  compares
    - label Extras (optional-dependencies)
      children
        - label Published in the wheel metadata
          desc Ships to every consumer to resolve
        - label Audience — your consumers
          desc mytool[postgres] is an opt-in feature flag
        - label Holds features
          desc Things consumers choose to enable
        - label pytest does not belong here
          desc A test extra pollutes consumer resolutions
    - label Dependency groups (PEP 735)
      children
        - label Never published in the wheel
          desc Development-side only
        - label Audience — you, the developer
          desc dev = test runners, linters, type checkers
        - label Holds workflows
          desc uv installs the dev group by default
        - label Legacy fakes it with a dev extra
          desc A workaround that predates PEP 735
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
